            <title>[LU-21052] sanity test_252: extra mdtlov records on a one-MDT run</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21052</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_252 fails with:&lt;br/&gt;
Invalid number of mdtlov clients returned by /usr/sbin/lr_reader&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The review-ldiskfs run has one MDT: tests requiring &amp;gt;= 2 MDTs skip&lt;br/&gt;
throughout the sanity suite. lr_reader -c on MDT0000 nevertheless&lt;br/&gt;
prints all three records:&lt;br/&gt;
  lustre-MDT0001-mdtlov_UUID (generation 7)&lt;br/&gt;
  lustre-MDT0003-mdtlov_UUID (generation 8)&lt;br/&gt;
  lustre-MDT0002-mdtlov_UUID (generation 9)&lt;br/&gt;
The test counts these records and requires MDSCOUNT - 1, which is zero.&lt;br/&gt;
The origin of the extra records needs investigation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failing session (change 69752 PS8, revision 7aeb72a769b5):&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/f29fc202-c578-4f18-8b67-7442390637cd" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/f29fc202-c578-4f18-8b67-7442390637cd&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Failed test set:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/0c71231a-fdeb-46dc-abf7-8928b071816b" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/0c71231a-fdeb-46dc-abf7-8928b071816b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Test log:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/469be54e-349c-4f36-9778-196ee1c91057/show_text" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/469be54e-349c-4f36-9778-196ee1c91057/show_text&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This predates the PCC controls in change 69752. A lustre-master run&lt;br/&gt;
on 2026-04-30 has the same three MDT0001/2/3 records and assertion,&lt;br/&gt;
and its suite also skips tests requiring &amp;gt;= 2 MDTs:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/4ce18524-f764-4664-a4b7-21be04505a74" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/4ce18524-f764-4664-a4b7-21be04505a74&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/7ba45a73-8eaa-49b0-9073-32af765cebed/show_text" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/7ba45a73-8eaa-49b0-9073-32af765cebed/show_text&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Another lustre-master run on 2025-09-19 has the same three records:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/b3c60f97-cbda-49d5-be67-3d6a9491aa49" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/b3c60f97-cbda-49d5-be67-3d6a9491aa49&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/04d560db-02d5-4e24-937b-13874b3b4949/show_text" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_logs/04d560db-02d5-4e24-937b-13874b3b4949/show_text&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Change 69752 changes neither sanity.sh, lr_reader nor last_rcvd client&lt;br/&gt;
accounting. Its MDT checks apply only to PCC attach/create requests.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-13402" title="sanity test_252: Invalid number of mdtlov clients returned by /usr/sbin/lr_reader" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-13402"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-13402&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; has the same generic assertion but concerns a missing local&lt;br/&gt;
MDT0002 record. Here MDT0002 is present and there are too many records.&lt;br/&gt;
Its fix (38138) is already in the tested revision. Searches for the&lt;br/&gt;
test, assertion, lr_reader and mdtlov clients found no covering ticket.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rainshadow reports one test_252 failure in 4563 review-ldiskfs runs&lt;br/&gt;
in 30 days, and two occurrences of this assertion in 18482 master&lt;br/&gt;
suite runs over two years across configurations. These are rare-event&lt;br/&gt;
counts, not a measured rate for a confirmed root cause. No local&lt;br/&gt;
reproduction was attempted; the branch logs establish independence&lt;br/&gt;
from this patch and occasional passes would not resolve the defect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69752-ps8-fc4955db1648 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69752" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69752&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
